# tests/services_runtime.rs::durable_lifecycle_matrix_covers_all_delivery_scenarios_on_all_tiers: the original's literal expectations with one hand-derived correction.
# Fixture migrated: `partition_done:Delivered:4`, not the original `:3`. The partitioned retry appends its Accepted event (attempt 1) before its enqueue meets the partition, so the history is accept, retry, Delivering, Delivered (Rust ServiceAuthority.rs 3050-3086 appends before enqueue; delivery_event_signature 2252-2296 never consults the registry; Core/Service/Service.jet runtime_retry).
# Fixture migrated: the original 60-second retention is 3600 seconds. On a loaded host the run passed 60 seconds, so live entries expired and receive found an empty mailbox. The expiry scenario keeps its own 1 ms runtime.
fixture: durable_lifecycle_matrix_covers_all_delivery_scenarios_on_all_tiers/input
# D-SERVICE-EFFECTS1=A: the durable service calls reach FS.Read and FS.Write.
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read,FS.Write run.jet
exit: 0 # tests/services_runtime.rs:2334 assert_tiers_agree
stdout: = "accept:Accepted\nduplicate:true:Accepted\nconflict:Policy\ndelivered:accepted\nretention:true:3:Delivered\nretry_first:retry\nretry_state:Accepted:true:3\nretry_second:retry\nretry_done:Delivered\ncancel:Cancelled\ndead:DeadLettered\nexpiry:DeadLettered:2\npartition:Partitioned\npartition_recovery:Accepted\npartition_delivery:partition\npartition_done:Delivered:4\nrevoked:Revoked\n" # tests/services_runtime.rs:2334 assert_tiers_agree
